Apache License 2.0 §4(b) — modified-file notice
================================================

Every file under strix/ (the Python package) is a modified work relative to
Strix v1.0.4 (OmniSecure Inc., Apache-2.0). Samtek applied the Recon
control-plane patches listed in the recon repo's docs/strix-fork-patches.md
on top of the upstream v1.0.4 tag; the package name is kept as `strix` to
minimise merge cost against future upstream releases (an earlier version of
this fork had renamed the package to `reconcore`; that rename was reverted
2026-09-20 as part of the upstream-merge-mechanism work).

This file is the catalog of change classes. Every modified source file under
strix/ and containers/docker-entrypoint.sh also carries a one-line "Modified
by Samtek" banner (Apache License 2.0 §4(b)). CI fails if a strix/*.py file
is missing that banner. Do not present strix/ as unmodified upstream Strix,
and do not drop LICENSE.

Material classes of change (not an exhaustive git path list):

- Product rebrand: operator-visible strings say "Recon"; CLI entry is `recon`;
  sandbox image is `recon-sandbox`. The internal Python package stays `strix`
  (matches upstream, easier merges).
- Browser CLI alias: agent-browser → recon-browser (image symlink + prompts).
- Env/config: STRIX_* / RECON_STRIX_* → RECON_* / RECON_ENGINE_*.
- Telemetry: vendor analytics hard-off.
- Containment: RECON_EGRESS_PROXY in front of Caido; k8s sandbox client;
  sandboxnet destination-pinned egress; gVisor/runtime-class wiring;
  Sandbox CRD adoption hooks.
- Auth preflight / mailbox / host-side session contracts.
- Vulnerability report screenshots and extra_env credential injection.
- Skills, prompts, and system text rewritten for the Recon operator model.
- Rebased onto upstream v1.6.2 on 2026-09-20 (was v1.0.4). Brings 13 minor
  upstream releases of new capability. Adopted upstream skills (OAuth, AWS,
  Django, insecure_deserialization, prototype_pollution, OWASP LLM Top 10,
  Azure/Entra, AD/Kerberos, argument injection, ecosystem supply-chain,
  Hurl/Hypothesis, semantic browser, Electron, Grafana/Prometheus,
  weak-password, GCP+Auth0 recon, Firebase storage rules) and upstream's
  SARIF+STRIDE emitter, replacing our v1.0.4-era vendored copies. The MCP
  server module (strix/tools/mcp/, added in upstream v1.6.0) is present in
  the tree because upstream code (agents/factory, core/runner, TUI) imports
  it structurally; it is disabled at runtime in Recon deployments by
  configuration (no MCP servers registered) rather than by structural
  deletion — see docs/CAPABILITIES.md for the deferred structural-exclude
  work. The pinned agent-SDK / provider / router dep triple (openai-agents
  ==0.14.6 / openai==2.44.0 / litellm==1.90.3) is intentionally held at the
  T11 Vertex-baseline pins pending a live-run re-validation.

containers/Dockerfile is also modified (tool pins, strix/ COPY paths).
scripts/ and packaging files in this directory are modified for the rebrand.
